COLUMNS
int ID
string Name // the liquid type's name ("Water", "Ocean", "Magma", "Slime", "Slow Water", ...): proven from the bytes
string Texture // six texture path templates per type; slot 0 names the animated frames ("XTextures\river\lake_a.%d.blp" gives lake_a.1.blp to lake_a.N.blp, N its FrameCountTexture): proven from the bytes; what slots 1-5 are for is not established
int Field_02 // not established (bit-set-like values)
int SoundBank // the type's kind -- 0 water, 1 ocean, 2 magma, 3 slime on the four base rows and on every variant of each, and MLIQ's vertex form follows it: proven from the bytes (the name is the public definitions'; nothing about sound is established)
int Field_04 // not established
int Field_05 // not established
float Field_06 // not established
float Field_07 // not established
float Field_08 // not established
float Field_09 // not established
int Field_10 // not established (16 bits: its pallet words carry a constant upper half)
float Field_11 // not established
int Field_12 // not established
int Field_13 // not established
int MaterialID // a LiquidMaterial row: every value is one, in every client (proven from the bytes)
int MinimapStaticCol // a colour, 0xAARRGGBB as stored (water 0x9F12A0D5, magma 0xFFD06800, slime 0xFF4ABA3C): a colour proven from the bytes; that it is the minimap's is inferred
int FrameCountTexture // per Texture slot, the frames of a %d template in the low byte (30 for lake_a, 16 for fast_a; lake_a.31.blp does not exist): proven from the bytes; the pallet's upper 24 bits are a constant that is not part of the value
int Field_17 // not established (colour-like)
float Float // floats: proven from the bytes; what the first two are for is inferred, not proven
int Field_19 // not established
float Field_20 // not established

COMMENT Written for WoW Model Viewer's liquid catalogue (wow::LiquidCatalog, docs/world-viewer/09-liquids.md 1.4). The
COMMENT layout comes from public table definitions, read as hypotheses: every column the catalogue reads (database.xml,
COMMENT table LiquidType) was checked against the four clients' own bytes, and only those columns carry established
COMMENT meanings; the others are named by their field index, their types and widths the hypotheses' (never read). Every
COMMENT field is listed in file order, so the positions are right for the layout below. Its hash is the same in Retail
COMMENT 12.1.5, Classic Era 1.15.9, MoP Classic 5.5.4 and Classic Beta 1.60.1. A layout not listed here is not read.

LAYOUT D1ECEEC9
BUILD 12.1.5.70448, 1.15.9.70003, 5.5.4.70449, 1.60.1.70450
